@tradition lap-of-the-wren
// Sundays 20:30 (playtest 1: moved off Monday), host Tomas. A slow walk round the promenade (Deck 3), chatting.
== mail
- Lap of the Wren at {time}: one slow walk round the promenade. No pace, no rules, just company.
== ask
- Lap of the Wren tonight? It's just walking. And gossip.   #funny
- Walk the promenade with us later? Slow as you like.
== here
- Slower, slower. It's not a race. It's a stroll.   #funny
- Look at the stars from this side. Different, isn't it?
- One lap, then tea. That's the deal.
== thanks
- You join the slow walk round the promenade. People fall into step, chat, and drift between groups as the stars slide past.
== chatter
- Lap of the Wren's the best bit of a Sunday.
- I walk the lap to stretch my legs and my ears.   #funny
- Sunday lap tonight. Bring someone new.
